        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "The full Theorem2.4 and Proposition4.1 core are included, restricted to lambda=1/m, m a positive integer, with c>-1 and Q(zeta)=|zeta|^(2/m)-(2c/N)log|zeta|, at the singular origin with the exact micro-scale(2.13). Existing radial skew-polynomial/Pfaffian representation theory and the standard Mittag-Leffler homogeneous solutions are background; the new gamma-product system, scaling and inhomogeneous normalization are supplied. Arbitrary fractional-order claims of4.1 are only context, not a separate selected result. The author permits branch changes as cocycles preserving correlation functions; no single-valued pre-kernel is asserted. The proof last displayed line keeps a tilde W symbol after extracting F although(4.14) defines that tilde as already containing F. Preserve this local display literally with the editorial note: the preceding integral formula and explicit(4.14) give the claimed statement without any missing core or replacement argument."
